{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "41d5a992-673f-491e-b912-a55334e4dfec"/*ImageSegmentationExample*/,
  "Description": "Segments a live camera image into known categories (background, hair, body-skin, face-skin, clothes, others) and tints the segmented region with a color: the camera image is fed into both inputs of [BlendWithMask], whose [Mask] input receives the [ImageSegmentation] mask - so everything the model segments is tinted magenta. Change [ColorB] for a different tint, or wire a custom image into [ImageB].\n\nThe raw segmentation outputs are available directly: [MaskTexture] is the binary category mask of [Model]'s selected category, [CategoryMask] holds all categories, and [ConfidenceMask]/[Confidence] the per-pixel confidence. [SelectedCategories] picks which categories count as foreground.",
  "InputUis": [],
